 "details": {
  "title": "I’ve Never Been in Love Before",
  "lead": "The tune for trumpet in A♭ (B♭ for the trumpet), concert A♭3 to F5, a slow ballad, set on the bars of the Fret Finder guitar arrangement, which follows the record a whole step down. That page counts the ballad in eighths, so each bar of the lead sheet takes two of its bars and the notes are written twice as long. A short line of our own opens it on the tune’s last phrase, then the whole song as the singer has it, held notes and all (the page calls its first half the verse), the trumpet solo from that page, the song’s second half again with the last line stretched, and the page’s closing line over the last three bars.",
